{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" Pod That Asked\n\nLook back at what you did in this chapter, and notice that you only ever asked one question.\n\n*Does the file survive the container restart?* *Does the volume survive the Pod?* *Does the claim survive the workload?* *Does the data survive the claim?* Four questions, one"}},"session_id":"a302764d-f2ca-47b0-919a-f922ff4754ea","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"e4a10cf6-beee-4d87-ac84-34d18f8eeff5"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" shape: **what survives what?** Every section widened the scope by exactly one step, and the ladder in §1 was the whole chapter drawn small.\n\nHere is what makes it worth the walk. At every rung, the thing that would seem to have the most at stake in the answ"}},"session_id":"a302764d-f2ca-47b0-919a-f922ff4754ea","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"8a4cbb93-2dea-4712-b427-f2221890d6dc"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"er is not the thing that decides it.\n\nThe container does not decide whether its files survive a restart. The image layout decided that, before the container existed. The Pod does not decide whether its volume survives deletion; the volume's *"}},"session_id":"a302764d-f2ca-47b0-919a-f922ff4754ea","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"0dff99c2-3ee8-4256-bd5f-989c121d4a0e"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"type* decided it, chosen in a manifest by whoever wrote the PodSpec. And the claim does not decide whether the data survives the claim's deletion. The StorageClass decided that, in a `reclaimPolicy` field, in a"}},"session_id":"a302764d-f2ca-47b0-919a-f922ff4754ea","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"272fca14-8217-47c5-97ad-7687098ba8f3"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" manifest written by an administrator who was configuring a cluster and had never heard of your application.\n\nThe workload never gets a vote. That is not a defect. It is the same separation that runs through everything you have learned:\n\nA Pod does not decide which node it lands on; the scheduler does"}},"session_id":"a302764d-f2ca-47b0-919a-f922ff4754ea","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"df42f014-3adb-4b90-bca3-265da02e71c0"}
